    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="0794" n="790" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/15245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Myers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-22T13:00:00+08:00">July 22, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 22—12:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. The Japanese Consul General has informed me that the Pearl River will be
                    closed to all navigation, due to military reasons, for about <pb facs="0795"
                        n="791" xml:id="pg791"/> 2 weeks probably from night of July 24. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mindanao</hi><anchor n="16" xml:id="d780-f1"/> has been
                    informed.</p>
                <p>There is reason to believe the military operations indicated will take place in
                    the West River and Pearl River deltas as there has been considerable fighting in
                    that general area recently. Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d780-f1" n="16" xml:id="d780-f1-content">
                <p>United States gunboat of the South China Patrol, U. S. Asiatic Fleet.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
